*.pyc
.DS_Store
FIRE_LOG*.jsonl
SURGERY_LOG.jsonl
audit-output.txt

# Vendor skill packs: machine-local, reinstalled per machine, never committed
# (DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-10). Kept in step with the VENDOR sets in
# hooks/check-index.mjs and hooks/audit-fires.mjs; check-index.test.mjs
# asserts all three sites agree.
agents-sdk/
cloudflare/
cloudflare-email-service/
cloudflare-one/
cloudflare-one-migrations/
durable-objects/
sandbox-migrate-to-next/
sandbox-next/
sandbox-stable/
turnstile-spin/
web-perf/
workers-best-practices/
wrangler/

# The claude.ai skill-sync cache, written by the desktop app: a bucket directory
# named <orgId>_<userId> holding the anthropic-example skills (docx, pdf, pptx,
# xlsx, morning, import-memory, ash-training-roster) plus a manifest. 222 files as
# of 2026-09-21, including ISO-IEC 29500 .xsd schemas and a .woff2, none of it this
# library's content. Same rule as the vendor block above (DECISIONS.md 2026-08-10):
# not ours, so never committed, indexed or counted.
#
# Deliberately NOT a member of the VENDOR sets in check-index.mjs and
# audit-fires.mjs. Those count top-level directories that hold a SKILL.md, and this
# one's skills are nested a level down, so the index gate never sees it -- it
# reports 46 and passes with synced/ on disk. Adding it to those sets would claim a
# collision that does not exist.
synced/

# cross-agent-review: scaffolding travels, transcripts and local seat state do not
exchange/**
!exchange/README.md
!exchange/PROTOCOL.md
!exchange/TEMPLATE_REVIEW.md
!exchange/kickoffs/
!exchange/kickoffs/**


# org-skill upload artefacts, rebuilt from source on demand
org-skills/*.zip
